+The payload limit is 64 MiB, and a record over it is refused before anything is written. Valid UTF-8 cannot contain the byte `FB`.
+
+### Reading, and the end of the log
+
+A reader scans frames from the start. If it meets bytes that are not a complete, checksummed frame, it looks for any valid frame after them. If there is one, acknowledged data is damaged and the reader raises `CorruptLogError` with the offset and changes nothing. If there is none, the bytes are a write that was cut off (partial, zero-filled, or with a bad checksum). The process holding the lock cuts them off the file before it writes anything else. A frame with a good checksum whose payload is not JSON is always damage.
 
